  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A pizza tray was measured to be $28.6\\text{ m}$ in diameter.\nWhat is the lower and upper limit for the area of the pizza tray? Give your answers to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Lower limit: $640.18\\text{ m}^2$; upper limit: $644.72\\text{ m}^2$. Use diameter limits $28.55\\text{ m}$ and $28.65\\text{ m}$ in $A=\\pi(\\frac{d}{2})^2$.",
      "worked": "Precision: $0.1\\text{ m}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Absolute error}&=\\tfrac12\\times0.1=0.05\\text{ m}\\\\d_{\\text{lower}}&=28.6-0.05=28.55\\text{ m}\\\\d_{\\text{upper}}&=28.6+0.05=28.65\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $A=\\pi r^2$ and $r=\\frac{d}{2}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{lower}}&=\\pi\\left(\\frac{28.55}{2}\\right)^2\\\\A_{\\text{lower}}&\\approx640.18\\text{ m}^2\\\\A_{\\text{upper}}&=\\pi\\left(\\frac{28.65}{2}\\right)^2\\\\A_{\\text{upper}}&\\approx644.72\\text{ m}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
